WEBVTT

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:07.230
Again...

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:15.260
It was probably her thoughts and memories 
flowing into you through magical power.

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:17.030
Through magical power?

00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:19.340
As I told you before,

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:23.080
all the magical power in the 
world is gathered in that space.

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:26.330
The concentration of 
magic is extremely dense.

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:30.010
That magic responds to our wills,

00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:31.630
creating the ARMANOX.

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:36.270
And through the ARMANOX, we use techniques

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:39.600
to control that magical power and fight.

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:44.540
So you're saying we all use this energy 
that's like one big magic source

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:47.210
to fight each other?

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:49.850
That's a fair assessment.

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:54.950
You could also say we're all connected 
to Magiaconatus through magic.

00:00:55.510 --> 00:00:57.450
So why are we fighting, then?

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:04.680
I mean, there's this enormous power, 
and each of us can use it, right?

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:07.330
Do we really need to fight, in that case?

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:10.350
That's what Magiaconatus wants.

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:14.480
It desires the one and only 
mage capable of obtaining it,

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:16.090
or so they say.

00:01:21.830 --> 00:01:23.140
Nene-chan?

00:01:23.570 --> 00:01:25.500
What are you so surprised about?

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:27.980
Did you think I was dead?

00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:45.000
<b>GRANBELM</b>

00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:44.870
The Two Princeps

00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:00.920
I knew I'd be butting in,

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:04.280
but I wanted to know more about 
the mages that defeated me.

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:06.240
Oh...

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:09.000
What mage family are you 
from? What's your surname?

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:11.370
Kohinata...

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:15.680
Kohinata? Never heard of them.

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:18.560
Are they Scandinavian? East Asian?

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:20.340
Wait, are they independent?

00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:23.710
Will you get over your surprise already?!

00:03:23.710 --> 00:03:27.260
The only thing you lose by being defeated 
in GRANBELM is the right to battle!

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:28.720
You didn't even know that?

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:31.940
It's not that... This is...

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:34.310
...the high school building.

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:36.370
What's going on?

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:40.740
Wh-What are you staring at?!

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:41.610
Stop!

00:03:42.350 --> 00:03:43.660
Hi there!

00:03:43.850 --> 00:03:46.530
Thanks for taking care of Nene-nee!

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:49.290
It's the middle school that takes 
care of Nene-nee, not here.

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:53.040
Nene... nee?

00:03:53.970 --> 00:03:56.650
Anyway, I can't believe you 
don't know your own lineage.

00:03:56.650 --> 00:03:59.380
And yet you can still wield 
so much magical power.

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:02.290
I guess there's still a lot we don't know

00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:04.800
about both GRANBELM and Magiaconatus.

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:10.120
In fact, we've been told that <i>this</i> aspect of 
Nene-nee is due to the influence of magic.

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:11.400
Get your hand off me!

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:15.100
I guess magic spells will always be 
a challenging research subject...

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:16.270
Nene-chan!

00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:20.480
There you are! Over here, Kibou!

00:04:20.890 --> 00:04:22.040
You're...

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:25.800
These are my younger sisters, Mimi and Nana.

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:27.240
Huh?

00:04:27.860 --> 00:04:29.850
What a cutie! Who is this?

00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:34.810
Well, in a word, she's... 
my best friend, I suppose.

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:41.050
Anyway, if there's anything you 
don't understand, just ask.

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:42.970
I'll help you.

00:04:42.970 --> 00:04:44.590
Huh? You will?

00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:46.180
But, why?

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:50.430
I want to see the moment 
the one and only true mage,

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:53.180
the Witch, is born.

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:58.010
The Witch...

00:05:03.270 --> 00:05:09.620
I'll show you that I'm 
qualified to be the Witch!

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:17.080
Onee-sama...

00:05:18.530 --> 00:05:19.710
Please...

00:05:23.730 --> 00:05:26.300
Give me power!

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:29.220
Wow...

00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:39.000
I did it...

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:43.190
Ernesta... I did it!

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:44.280
Yes.

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:48.810
My mother and grandmother couldn't even 
perform that technique, and I did it!

00:05:48.810 --> 00:05:50.410
I did it!

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:51.660
That's great.

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:58.940
I can become the one and 
only true mage, can't I?

00:05:58.940 --> 00:06:01.840
I can be... the Witch!

00:06:02.350 --> 00:06:04.460
Yes... I'm sure you can.

00:06:07.240 --> 00:06:15.000
The puppet show begins on a moonlit night...

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:22.650
A puppet show in which 
only one puppet is real...

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:24.670
What's that song?

00:06:24.670 --> 00:06:27.000
It's an old nursery rhyme.

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:28.980
I've never heard it before.

00:06:28.980 --> 00:06:30.650
How does it end?

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:36.290
The last remaining puppet puts 
its hands together and prays

00:06:36.290 --> 00:06:39.210
that the puppet show might last forever.

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:45.680
The puppet show has begun.
It's begun again in the next town.

00:06:46.270 --> 00:06:47.760
Oh...

00:06:50.750 --> 00:06:51.730
Suishou!

00:06:51.730 --> 00:06:53.120
What's the matter?

00:06:53.120 --> 00:06:54.180
Look!

00:06:57.050 --> 00:07:00.430
So there really is a darkness approaching.

00:07:00.430 --> 00:07:01.630
Darkness?

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:03.920
Yes...

00:07:04.420 --> 00:07:08.950
This household's guardian spirit 
is saying danger is on the way.

00:07:11.180 --> 00:07:12.320
What are you doing?

00:07:12.520 --> 00:07:15.330
If you would listen to me, 
I wouldn't have done it!

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:22.020
I'm listening, but I believe 
that discussion is long over.

00:07:22.020 --> 00:07:24.330
I wasn't given a satisfactory explanation!

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:27.310
At the family meeting—

00:07:26.410 --> 00:07:29.510
Who gave you permission to speak?! Be quiet!

00:07:29.510 --> 00:07:30.320
Anna!

00:07:35.950 --> 00:07:37.850
As you are aware,

00:07:38.280 --> 00:07:42.200
the larger a magic stone grows, 
the more difficult it is to use.

00:07:42.760 --> 00:07:47.620
Magiaconatus is a space surrounded 
by extremely dense magical power.

00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:49.900
If the user isn't skilled enough...

00:07:51.430 --> 00:07:55.030
The magical power within 
the stone will go berserk.

00:07:55.230 --> 00:07:56.640
Are you saying I'm unskilled—

00:07:56.640 --> 00:07:59.330
I am not. I'm saying...

00:07:59.890 --> 00:08:00.910
What?

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:06.200
I participated in GRANBELM with the 
smallest magic stone in this family,

00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:08.250
and I made it as far as the final five!

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:13.590
I believe I'm more than qualified to use 
the Fugo magic stone instead of this one!

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:17.600
But Ernesta is still in 
the battle, is she not?

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:21.730
Why must you bring up Ernesta now?

00:08:22.040 --> 00:08:28.280
Ernesta has progressed to this point with the
 tiny shard of magic stone you gave her long ago.

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:32.240
Even with the magic stone you 
have, you couldn't defeat her.

00:08:33.640 --> 00:08:36.460
Even if you used the Fugo magic stone,

00:08:36.460 --> 00:08:39.200
you could not defeat Ernesta.

00:08:39.350 --> 00:08:42.630
She is favored by magical power.

00:08:42.630 --> 00:08:46.130
You could say she has received 
the blessing of the gods.

00:08:46.130 --> 00:08:50.320
To deny that would mean 
defying the gods themselves.

00:08:53.430 --> 00:08:54.850
You're wrong...

00:08:55.590 --> 00:08:57.760
You're wrong! You're wrong! You're wrong!

00:08:57.760 --> 00:08:58.470
You're wrong!

00:08:58.470 --> 00:08:59.630
Anna!

00:09:00.110 --> 00:09:02.300
Even as such a young child,

00:09:02.300 --> 00:09:06.560
I succeeded in using the technique 
you and Grandmother couldn't perform!

00:09:07.260 --> 00:09:11.400
If I could use the Fugo
magic stone, I know I could...

00:09:14.310 --> 00:09:15.720
Onee-sama...

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:17.770
Well, then...

00:09:19.720 --> 00:09:24.040
Nene-chan told me it was a big house, 
but this is bigger than I expected.

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:29.750
The Tsuchimikados are one of 
Japan's most famous mage families.

00:09:33.440 --> 00:09:34.310
Um...

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:36.570
Why...

00:09:42.020 --> 00:09:45.780
We didn't know you had a cold. 
Sorry for showing up unannounced.

00:09:45.780 --> 00:09:46.730
It's all right.

00:09:46.730 --> 00:09:52.210
It's common for mages who use 
powerful magic to become unwell...

00:09:53.490 --> 00:09:55.530
So, what brings you here?

00:09:55.530 --> 00:09:58.430
We thought we should come and thank you

00:09:58.430 --> 00:10:00.150
for your help in that last battle.

00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:03.330
We couldn't have won without your help.

00:10:04.480 --> 00:10:05.700
Is this necessary?

00:10:05.990 --> 00:10:06.690
Huh?

00:10:07.480 --> 00:10:10.290
We'll be fighting against 
each other next time.

00:10:12.630 --> 00:10:13.960
That is true.

00:10:15.280 --> 00:10:17.410
Mangetsu, let's go.

00:10:17.410 --> 00:10:19.550
Okay, but...

00:10:19.930 --> 00:10:21.880
I just made all this...

00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:27.230
Like it? Since you have a cold, I made 
my special ginger sauce for dipping!

00:10:27.510 --> 00:10:28.740
It's okay.

00:10:28.740 --> 00:10:30.100
I figured...

00:10:30.470 --> 00:10:33.230
I had no idea you lived by yourself.

00:10:34.390 --> 00:10:37.940
I'm not by myself. My older sister is here.

00:10:38.390 --> 00:10:41.870
She can't even eat meals 
with me now, though...

00:10:42.570 --> 00:10:44.270
I see.

00:10:44.270 --> 00:10:46.490
Why not? Is she sick?

00:10:48.970 --> 00:10:49.880
She's cursed.

00:10:53.050 --> 00:10:57.720
I have to become a mage 
so I can undo her curse.

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:05.180
I guess everyone has their own reasons 
why they can't afford to lose.

00:11:07.460 --> 00:11:08.830
What's the matter?

00:11:09.720 --> 00:11:11.680
I feel bad, kinda.

00:11:12.110 --> 00:11:16.530
I'm the only one who doesn't really have 
a strong wish or reason or anything,

00:11:16.810 --> 00:11:21.120
but I jumped in while the battle 
was ongoing and ended up winning...

00:11:21.120 --> 00:11:23.620
I tried to stop you.

00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:26.380
Yeah... I know.

00:11:26.920 --> 00:11:28.530
Do you regret all this?

00:11:31.150 --> 00:11:32.740
It's strange, you know?

00:11:32.740 --> 00:11:36.190
Going to that other space 
and controlling WHITE LILY,

00:11:36.190 --> 00:11:40.590
fighting and attacking the way 
I envision it in my mind...

00:11:40.590 --> 00:11:43.970
The better I get, the happier I feel.

00:11:44.400 --> 00:11:46.980
It's like, "Wow, I can do this!"

00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:49.660
I'm doing something other people can't do!

00:11:50.080 --> 00:11:52.760
And it's just so thrilling...

00:11:52.760 --> 00:11:57.940
Even now, I'm counting down the days 
in my head until the next battle.

00:11:59.480 --> 00:12:05.340
Long ago, when Magiaconatus was 
discovered and GRANBELM began,

00:12:05.340 --> 00:12:07.950
it was said that many mages asked

00:12:08.400 --> 00:12:10.910
why this battle had begun...

00:12:11.850 --> 00:12:16.350
and why Magiaconatus sought just one mage.

00:12:17.050 --> 00:12:18.170
And why is it?

00:12:19.590 --> 00:12:20.810
I don't know.

00:12:21.540 --> 00:12:25.740
But there are some mages who say this:

00:12:25.740 --> 00:12:30.970
"We mages control these dolls in 
order to obtain magical power,

00:12:30.970 --> 00:12:32.220
but it may be..."

00:12:33.460 --> 00:12:34.690
So cold...

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:44.580
"...that we are the ones being controlled."

00:12:48.430 --> 00:12:49.930
Master!

00:12:50.440 --> 00:12:51.290
What?

00:12:52.550 --> 00:12:55.500
Sorry, but I'm not gonna 
be your disciple anymore.

00:12:57.970 --> 00:13:01.870
I thought you had incredible 
strength, but I was so wrong!

00:13:01.870 --> 00:13:05.210
Ernesta's <i>way</i> stronger than you are.

00:13:05.210 --> 00:13:07.680
Why are you speaking in that tone?

00:13:10.100 --> 00:13:13.600
This is how I normally speak.

00:13:24.580 --> 00:13:28.320
You should just disappear already, loser.

00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:30.900
You're a weakling with no magical power.

00:13:41.400 --> 00:13:42.580
That girl...

00:13:44.440 --> 00:13:45.300
Shingetsu!

00:13:47.880 --> 00:13:49.800
Please, come back to us!

00:13:50.740 --> 00:13:51.840
Clare...

00:13:51.840 --> 00:13:54.240
Onee-sama is in trouble!

00:13:54.240 --> 00:13:57.260
She hasn't come out of the 
basement in five days!

00:13:58.480 --> 00:14:02.150
Please! I'll go with you to talk to her!

00:14:02.340 --> 00:14:04.730
I'll make sure you can patch things up!

00:14:07.110 --> 00:14:08.260
Shingetsu!

00:14:21.800 --> 00:14:23.920
You did talk to her, after all.

00:14:25.640 --> 00:14:30.240
And being honest with her didn't 
work, right, Shingetsu-chan?

00:14:31.830 --> 00:14:32.770
Hey, you know...

00:14:36.120 --> 00:14:39.620
Sorry for inviting myself over like this.

00:14:39.620 --> 00:14:40.650
It's all right.

00:14:40.650 --> 00:14:44.480
If you want to be left alone, 
just tell me, and I'll go.

00:14:47.560 --> 00:14:51.170
I kind of understand how you feel,

00:14:51.170 --> 00:14:54.190
but this sort of thing 
is really all I can do.

00:14:54.680 --> 00:14:58.130
This is just like when we 
went to see Kuon-chan, huh?

00:14:58.840 --> 00:15:00.120
Mangetsu...

00:15:00.840 --> 00:15:04.960
You know, for a long time, all 
my dreams have been pure white.

00:15:06.080 --> 00:15:07.900
There's nothing in them.

00:15:07.900 --> 00:15:12.890
I can't tell if I'm falling or
 floating, or anything else...

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:18.350
But all the nothingness makes me feel 
anxious and scared... So scared.

00:15:19.780 --> 00:15:21.750
When I wake up in the morning,

00:15:22.590 --> 00:15:24.360
I see there's nothing in my dreams, either.

00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:27.320
That's not true.

00:15:30.260 --> 00:15:32.430
You have a heart.

00:15:33.110 --> 00:15:35.290
A heart that can care for others.

00:15:42.940 --> 00:15:45.560
Do you like yourself, Shingetsu-chan?

00:15:46.020 --> 00:15:47.930
No, I don't.

00:15:48.340 --> 00:15:53.390
But lately, I've started to think that 
very few people really like themselves.

00:15:54.770 --> 00:15:55.910
Really?

00:15:55.910 --> 00:15:56.510
Yeah.

00:15:57.200 --> 00:16:02.730
I think everyone has an ideal version 
of themselves within their hearts,

00:16:03.250 --> 00:16:07.320
but most of the time, their real 
selves can't catch up to it.

00:16:07.750 --> 00:16:08.940
Yeah, maybe...

00:16:09.800 --> 00:16:12.650
Perhaps that's why we grow up

00:16:12.650 --> 00:16:15.780
and try to look ahead to the future.

00:16:16.420 --> 00:16:18.860
I wonder if we'll ever catch up...

00:16:19.420 --> 00:16:21.440
I doubt it.

00:16:21.440 --> 00:16:24.280
I think we'll spend our 
lives chasing that ideal.

00:16:26.440 --> 00:16:28.960
Being alive isn't easy...

00:16:31.910 --> 00:16:34.150
Is that so bad, though?

00:16:34.670 --> 00:16:36.450
From the universe's perspective,

00:16:36.450 --> 00:16:39.720
the few decades we spend living 
here might as well be seconds.

00:16:40.330 --> 00:16:42.610
And what's a few seconds of suffering?

00:16:43.220 --> 00:16:44.340
I see...

00:16:44.880 --> 00:16:46.860
You're so smart, Shingetsu-chan.

00:16:52.170 --> 00:16:56.800
A long time ago, Anna cooked for me, too.

00:16:56.800 --> 00:17:01.090
I had a cold, and she wanted to 
make something German for me,

00:17:01.090 --> 00:17:02.480
so she made mashed potatoes.

00:17:06.850 --> 00:17:10.550
Mangetsu, would you mind accompanying me?

00:17:16.930 --> 00:17:18.090
Of course...

00:17:18.310 --> 00:17:22.430
There's barely any magic here. How could
I possibly strengthen the magic stone?

00:17:25.340 --> 00:17:26.240
Are you sure?

00:17:26.730 --> 00:17:27.900
Let's go.

00:17:30.550 --> 00:17:31.680
Come in.

00:17:33.200 --> 00:17:34.610
Ernesta!

00:17:35.430 --> 00:17:39.000
Please forgive this sudden intrusion, ma'am.

00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:40.330
Are you back to stay?

00:17:43.680 --> 00:17:46.380
I've come to tell Anna the truth.

00:17:48.540 --> 00:17:52.990
I appreciate your kindness, but 
if this goes on, Anna will—

00:17:52.990 --> 00:17:55.170
Ernesta!

00:18:03.580 --> 00:18:05.060
Die!

00:18:07.720 --> 00:18:10.010
How could you...

00:18:10.010 --> 00:18:11.480
Why?!

00:18:11.790 --> 00:18:14.710
How could you ignore everything 
I said, and allow this...

00:18:14.710 --> 00:18:17.500
this <i>demon</i> to...

00:18:15.760 --> 00:18:16.780
Stop it!

00:18:22.010 --> 00:18:24.900
Even if it means hurting Anna,

00:18:24.900 --> 00:18:27.770
things cannot remain this way.

00:18:31.600 --> 00:18:36.220
Your mother didn't want to force 
you to bear the misfortune

00:18:36.220 --> 00:18:38.560
of living as this family's mage.

00:18:39.400 --> 00:18:44.020
She chose to adopt me out of love for you.

00:18:44.740 --> 00:18:48.540
What? The "misfortune" of living as a mage?

00:18:49.020 --> 00:18:50.310
Why is that misfortune?

00:18:50.310 --> 00:18:53.450
For one who lacks power, 
it is great misfortune.

00:18:53.860 --> 00:18:55.450
Mother...

00:18:55.450 --> 00:18:58.800
If you were to bear the burden of 
this family with the power you have,

00:18:58.800 --> 00:19:00.750
you would regret it.

00:19:00.750 --> 00:19:05.030
You would constantly feel powerless 
and inferior as a mage.

00:19:06.810 --> 00:19:08.850
That is all you can do.

00:19:12.180 --> 00:19:14.130
Why won't you believe in me?!

00:19:14.730 --> 00:19:16.920
Didn't I tell you before?!

00:19:16.920 --> 00:19:20.150
I successfully performed that technique!

00:19:20.150 --> 00:19:23.380
In a world that has lost 
nearly all of its magic,

00:19:23.380 --> 00:19:25.560
I succeeded, just like this!

00:19:31.340 --> 00:19:32.440
Wow...

00:19:32.640 --> 00:19:37.340
Well? Can you still claim I have no power?

00:19:37.340 --> 00:19:38.980
That I'm unqualified?

00:19:39.570 --> 00:19:42.450
You still haven't realized?

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:47.040
Why do you think you were successful

00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:51.800
at a technique that no one 
can ever perform alone?

00:20:06.830 --> 00:20:08.530
I shouldn't have done it.

00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:11.700
I truly am sorry.

00:20:13.110 --> 00:20:16.360
My deception took your hand,

00:20:17.200 --> 00:20:20.110
giving you power as you 
performed the technique.

00:20:24.580 --> 00:20:28.380
Ernesta loves you.

00:20:29.140 --> 00:20:35.320
She wanted to please you, to see 
you happy. That's all it was.

00:20:36.640 --> 00:20:40.800
You were not born under a star
 that would bless you as a mage.

00:20:41.790 --> 00:20:43.520
No matter how you wish for it,

00:20:43.520 --> 00:20:46.930
you don't have the power to use 
the techniques Ernesta does,

00:20:47.230 --> 00:20:50.680
nor will you ever be 
favored by magic as she is.

00:20:52.390 --> 00:20:55.080
But that's all.

00:20:55.080 --> 00:20:58.730
There are countless other stars, 
and countless other good fortunes.

00:20:59.350 --> 00:21:04.940
My wish is that you would dedicate 
yourself to making your own star shine.

00:21:19.310 --> 00:21:23.860
Seeing your feelings toward mages 
and your determination to be one

00:21:23.860 --> 00:21:26.720
taught me what it means to be a mage.

00:21:27.340 --> 00:21:32.110
I never would have been 
born as a mage without you.

00:21:33.200 --> 00:21:38.490
I will carry on your wishes as I strive
 to become the Princeps mage.

00:21:39.030 --> 00:21:42.330
While I do, please protect this family...

00:21:44.130 --> 00:21:46.060
by being something other than a mage.

00:22:04.230 --> 00:22:05.440
Ernesta...

00:22:12.240 --> 00:22:13.750
Please do your best.

00:22:14.210 --> 00:22:16.640
I know you'll achieve your goal.

00:22:22.680 --> 00:22:23.550
I will.

00:22:24.480 --> 00:22:26.990
<b>To Be Continued</b>

00:23:56.990 --> 00:23:59.750
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:58.570 --> 00:24:01.710
<i>It is because she loved her
 that her heart aches.</i>

00:24:02.150 --> 00:24:04.770
<i>It is because she loved her 
that her obsession grows.</i>

00:24:05.720 --> 00:24:07.880
<i>She wants to make Ernesta struggle.</i>

00:24:08.100 --> 00:24:10.800
<i>She wants to make Ernesta notice 
her so badly that it disgusts her.</i>

00:24:11.320 --> 00:24:16.640
<i>She has wagered everything on 
a way of life known as "stalking."</i>

00:24:17.900 --> 00:24:19.600
<i>Next time on </i>GRANBELM<i>,</i>

00:24:19.600 --> 00:24:21.350
<i>"Miss Ressentiment."</i>

00:24:19.600 --> 00:24:21.850
<b>Miss Ressentiment</b>

00:24:22.150 --> 00:24:25.060
<i>What is the meaning of 
"pure and innocent hatred"?</i>

00:24:27.040 --> 00:24:30.030
<b>Look forward to the next episode!</b>
